", \"reasoning\": \"Rule 1 fails on four families. (1) F04: its note slot has the member ' (after regrouping)', and the word regrouping is in this lc's NOT_YET_KNOWN list, so a gated word is printed in a hint. (2) F07: names is a noun from _EMOJI_NAMES or its plural, and the domain allows the singular member, so the template 'How many {names} are left?' can print a singular noun with the plural verb 'are' (for example apple with are). (3) F08: name uses the same singular-or-plural domain with no link to b, so b = 1 can print a plural noun, and b = 2 or 3 can print a singular noun. (4) F09: verb is one of is or are with no link to a, and a is always 10 or more, so the verb can disagree with the count; also the group families F11 to F15 print 10, 11, 12, 15 or 20 emoji with template_chosen_by_values empty and no link to a, so a stated count can sit beside a group of a different size. F02, F05 and F06 were checked for a subtrahend larger than the minuend; the result runs of F06 (0 to 3, 5, 7 to 14, 17 to 19) show no negative result in any observed render, so that pairing is not judged a fault. Clauses are all PRODUCIBLE by the families named above.\"}",
